{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>It is a guilt-offering.</b> Even though sometimes this offering is brought and he did not in fact stumble in that sin, the one who considers it should not suppose that he is thereby introducing unconsecrated food into the Temple courtyard — for it is indeed a guilt-offering in any event, even though he did not stumble in the sin regarding which the doubt arose. The reason is that <b>he has incurred guilt before YHWH</b>, in that he did not guard himself in the matter until a doubt arose."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:44.314915541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}